@startuml use-case
title Smart Campus study room booking - Use-case diagram

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor Student
actor Administrator

rectangle "Smart Campus Study Room Booking System" {
  usecase "Search Available Rooms" as UC_Search
  usecase "Book Room" as UC_Book
  usecase "Cancel Own Booking" as UC_Cancel
  usecase "Send Confirmation" as UC_Confirm
  usecase "Block Room" as UC_Block
  usecase "Unblock Room" as UC_Unblock
  usecase "Review Room Usage" as UC_Usage

  note right of UC_Book
    R1: future start, 0 < duration <= 2 h
    (US-06 = rejection flow when > 2 h)
    R2: no overlap with an active booking
    of the same room; bookings that only
    touch (end 12:00 / start 12:00) do
    NOT overlap
    R3: blocked room is refused
  end note

  note right of UC_Confirm
    R4. Never initiated by an actor;
    reached only via <<include>>.
  end note

  note right of UC_Block
    R3: a blocked room accepts
    no new bookings.
  end note

  note right of UC_Usage
    From the scenario text;
    no approved story yet.
  end note
}

' --- Student goals ---
Student -- UC_Search : US-01
Student -- UC_Book : US-02, US-06
Student -- UC_Cancel : US-03

' --- Administrator goals ---
' Both actors sit on the left of the boundary so every association runs
' left, and every note and <<include>> runs right: nothing crosses.
Administrator -- UC_Block : US-04
Administrator -- UC_Unblock : US-05
Administrator -- UC_Usage : scenario

' --- Includes ---
' why: R4 - every successful booking must produce a confirmation
UC_Book ..> UC_Confirm : <<include>>

' why: R4 - approved-stories.md maps US-03 to R4, so a successful cancellation confirms too
UC_Cancel ..> UC_Confirm : <<include>>

' No actor is associated with Send Confirmation: no actor initiates it.
@enduml